// A percent repeat over a staff+tab: the repeated iterations print ONLY the % sign
// on BOTH staves. The notation staff hides its notes and the tab must hide its fret
// digits the same way (their stems/beams are already suppressed) — otherwise the tab
// left bare, stemless fret digits sitting under the % sign.
//
// ⚠️ ABSOLUTE octave, and it has to stay that way. Written relative — which is what the
// file was until 2026-08-01 — every `,,` reads against the note BEFORE it, so this riff
// fell two octaves per note and ran a hundred ledger lines off the bottom of the page.
// Every one of the sixteen notes warned LYS5002 (below the tab's lowest string) and none
// of them reached the tab at all, so the book tested nothing it claims to. It also broke
// the beam sweep, which read the ledger rows as a dozen phantom staves. The other tab
// fixtures that spell their own octaves are written the same way.
octave absolute
part bl {
  clef bass
  tuning bass
  section A {
    a,,4\4 r8 g,,16 a,,\4 c, c, a,,8\4 g,, a,,\4 |
    repeat percent 3 { a,,4\4 r8 g,,16 a,,\4 c, c, a,,8\4 g,, a,,\4 | }
  }
}
form main { A }
score main {
  staff bl
  tab bl
}
